{"version":2,"commands":[{"yarnName":"scene_transition","definitionName":"SceneTransition","fileName":"Sunrise Studio/Assets/Scripts/YarnCommands.cs","documentation":"<<scene_transition \"Classroom\">>: does nothing when the location is this scene, so a node can open with the scene it belongs to. Otherwise it loads that scene and the dialogue never continues here: the rest of the node (such as a <<jump>>) is left to the next scene, which plays its own start node with YarnCutscene. Location names ignore case, spaces, and underscores, so \"music_room\" loads the MusicRoom scene. <<scene_transition \"Classroom\" \"door\">> also plays the Sounds entry \"door\" as the transition starts closing. It plays on the CircleTransition, so the sound is not cut off when this scene unloads.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":214,"character":4},"end":{"line":220,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"location","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"sound","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"advance_time","definitionName":"AdvanceTime","fileName":"Sunrise Studio/Assets/Scripts/YarnCommands.cs","documentation":"<<advance_time \"lunch\">>: covers the screen, switches the time slot (ActiveDuringTime objects follow), uncovers it.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":269,"character":4},"end":{"line":280,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"slot","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"fade","definitionName":"FadeCommand","fileName":"Sunrise Studio/Assets/Scripts/YarnCommands.cs","documentation":"<<fade>>: covers and uncovers the screen. <<fade \"out\">> and <<fade \"in\">> only log for now: the scene transitions next to them already cover and uncover the screen.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":284,"character":4},"end":{"line":289,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"direction","isParamsArray":